    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\ud83d\udd0d IDENTIFY \u2014 Asset & Risk Awareness\n\nIdentify all hardware, software, and assets connected to the network.  \n- Login to Nessus  \n- Initialize segments  \n- Discover assets  \n- Tag metadata  \n(NIST: ID.AM-1, ID.AM-2)\n\n\u2705 Nodes \n\nAUTH - Login to Nessus\n\nDISC - Initialize Network Segments\n\nDISC - Discover Assets\n\nAI - Process Assets\n",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        176
      ],
      "id": "6750be3c-9ece-43a9-ac14-bada35158e72",
      "name": "Sticky Note7"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f PROTECT \u2014 Baseline Security Control\n\nEstablish controls to limit or contain security events.  \n- Scheduled scans  \n- Role-based scan control  \n- Ensure credentials securely managed  \n(NIST: PR.AC-1, PR.PT-1)\n\n\u2705 Nodes \n\nTrigger - Scheduled Scan\n\nAUTH - Set API Token\n",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        560
      ],
      "id": "8fbf4b3c-64bc-434c-bfb0-67703cc04bda",
      "name": "Sticky Note9"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\ud83e\udde0 AI Calculate Risk phase",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 680,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1024,
        1408
      ],
      "id": "57e3f5b4-a165-44bd-909a-8e5f3672c3e2",
      "name": "Sticky Note10"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\ud83d\udea8 DETECT \u2014 Vulnerability & Threat Scan\n\nContinuously monitor to detect anomalies or security events.  \n- Asset split-out  \n- Scan via Nessus  \n- Process vulnerability data  \n(NIST: DE.CM-1, DE.CM-8)\n\n\u2705 Nodes:\n\nUTILS - Split Assets\n\nSCAN - Run Nessus\n\nSCAN - Process Vulnerabilities\n",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 2
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        880
      ],
      "id": "96fe73e8-db97-4b2f-b05b-9e3ebd3ad85e",
      "name": "Sticky Note11"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f RESPOND \u2014 Risk Intelligence & Alerts\n\nAnalyze, prioritize, and respond to detected threats.  \n- AI-based LEV scoring  \n- Triage vulnerabilities  \n- Trigger critical alerts  \n(NIST: RS.AN-1, RS.RP-1)\n\n\u2705 Nodes:\n\nAI - Risk Evaluation\n\nAI - Triage Vulnerabilities\n\nALERT - LEV Trigger",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        1248
      ],
      "id": "8186e2dc-55da-4057-871c-5eb4166c729f",
      "name": "Sticky Note12"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\ud83d\udd01 RECOVER \u2014 Reporting & Remediation Support\n\nDocument, communicate, and improve based on assessments.  \n- Generate summary  \n- Email report to team  \n- Export to Google Sheets  \n(NIST: RC.IM-1, RC.CO-1)\n\n\u2705 Nodes:\n\nREPORT - Generate Summary\n\nEXPORT - Save to Sheet\n\nSend Email\n\n",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        1616
      ],
      "id": "b1233777-7698-47c1-9f8b-c2735e329288",
      "name": "Sticky Note2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\nCyberScan presenting an evidence-based, industry-backed strategy:\n\nLEV metric enhances risk-based prioritization.\n\nCyberScan showcase the flaws in EPSS and how you overcome them.\n\nCyberScan align with federal cybersecurity directives (like BOD 22-01 and KEV compliance).\n\nThis makes CyberScan audit-friendly, policy-aligned, and modern\u2014something many companies care about.\n\n\n                                                                                                            \n\n\n\n\n| **1. Identify** | \u201c\ud83e\udde0 Threat Inventory & CVE Scope\u201d        | Maps to CVE enumeration; ensures CyberScan starts by identifying scope of all assets and their exposure, Based on NVD/CVE/EPSS\n                                                              \n\n| **2. Protect**  | \u201c\ud83d\udd10 Hardening & Patch Guidance\u201d          | Aligns with remediation prioritization from LEV + KEV lists. Focus on patch strategies & mitigation workflows.                  \n\n\n| **3. Detect**   | \u201c\ud83d\udef0\ufe0f Vulnerability Monitoring Logic\u201d      | Covers how CyberScan detects exploit attempts using EPSS predictions and LEV metric to find *likely exploited vulnerabilities*. \n\n\n| **4. Respond**  | \u201c\ud83d\udea8 Automated Risk Response\u201d             | Showcases logic for how CyberScan handles high-risk CVEs (KEV, LEV > 0.9), sending alerts or blocking actions.                  \n\n\n| **5. Recover**  | \u201c\u267b\ufe0f Learning & Improvement Loop\u201d         | Focus on logging, metrics, audit trail, and recurring updates using EPSS and NIST recommendations. Enables cyber resilience.    \n\n\n",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 1240,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        528,
        176
      ],
      "id": "65c883da-c0b1-4920-b585-f21d10fd9533",
      "name": "Sticky Note8"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\nCyberScan visually engaging within the n8n editor and align it with NIST cybersecurity framework stages",
        "height": 100,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -896,
